{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.DescentCocycleDeviation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.DescentCocycleDeviation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.YekutieliTriple"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.descent_cocycle_deviation_unobstructed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.descent_cocycle_deviation_unobstructed","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-cocycle-deviation.lean#L64-L75","doc":"When the coboundary vanishes globally, the cocycle deviation\nalso vanishes — the standard unobstructedness statement\n(`twisted_cocycle_unobstructed` in the Lake tree). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.descent_cocycle_deviation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.descent_cocycle_deviation","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-cocycle-deviation.lean#L44-L62","doc":"**Cocycle deviation at level n+1 is a twisted Čech 2-cocycle.**\n\nFor any `TwistedTwoCocycle` on `M`, the field `cocycleDeviation`\nrealises the level-`n+1` deviation, satisfying the twisted\ncondition\n\n  `coboundary p = a(p) · cocycleDeviation(p) · a(p)⁻¹`\n\nwhere `a(p) = triple.twoMorphisms p`.  This is exactly the\n`twisted_condition` field of the structure. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:descent-cocycle-deviation","label":"lem:descent-cocycle-deviation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/descent-cocycle-deviation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}